            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use complementary identities, write cot and tan in terms of sin and cos, then combine the fractions.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Using the complementary and negative-angle identities,\n$$\\begin{align*}E&=-\\frac{1}{\\cot\\theta+\\tan\\theta}+\\frac{1}{\\cot\\theta-\\tan\\theta}\\\\E&=-\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}}+\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}}\\\\E&=-\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta+\\frac{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\E&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta(1-\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)}{\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta}\\\\E&=\\frac{2\\sin^3\\theta\\cos\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original expression requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$, $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos^2\\theta\\ne\\sin^2\\theta$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
